          "Business income and expenses are generally reported through Schedule C with the owner’s individual return.",
      },
      {
        title: "Partnerships",
        text:
          "Form 1065 preparation and applicable Schedule K-1 reporting for partners.",
      },
      {
        title: "S Corporations",
        text:
          "Form 1120S preparation and applicable shareholder reporting.",
      },
      {
        title: "C Corporations",
        text:
          "Form 1120 preparation and related federal and state filing requirements.",
      },
      {
        title: "Limited Liability Companies",
        text:
          "The filing requirement depends on how the LLC is classified for federal and state tax purposes.",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    eyebrow: "What May Be Included",
    title: "Business Return Preparation May Involve",
    bullets: [
      "Business income",
      "Ordinary and necessary business expenses",
      "Cost of goods sold",
      "Contractor-payment information",
      "Vehicle use",
      "Home-office information",
      "Business assets",
      "Depreciation",
      "Estimated payments",
      "Shareholder or partner information",
      "Schedule K-1 preparation",
      "Applicable state filings",
      "Multi-state business activity",
      "Prior-year filing issues",
    ],
    note:
      "The exact scope depends on the business entity, filing requirements, ownership structure, states involved, and condition of the records provided.",
  },
  {
    eyebrow: "Record Preparation",
    title:
      "Organized Business Records Support Accurate Filing",
    paragraphs: [
      "Business owners should maintain records that support the income, expenses, assets, and owner-related activity reported on the return.",
      "Global Bash may request additional documentation depending on the entity and filing requirements.",
    ],
    bullets: [
      "Income received",
      "Business expenses",
      "Contractor payments",
      "Payroll information when applicable",
      "Business mileage and vehicle use",
      "Asset purchases",
      "Loans and financing",
      "Owner contributions and distributions",
      "Inventory",
      "Business activity in other states",
      "Prior-year balances",
    ],
  },
  {
    eyebrow: "Planning",
    title:
      "Tax Preparation and Planning Work Better Together",
    paragraphs: [
      "A business return reports activity that has already occurred. Tax planning helps business owners consider estimated payments, recordkeeping needs, major purchases, income timing, and other future decisions before the next filing deadline.",
      "Planning does not guarantee that taxes will be reduced. Its purpose is to help business owners understand possible consequences and prepare more effectively.",
    ],
    relatedLink: {
      label: "Explore Tax Planning Services",
      href: "/tax-services/tax-planning/",
    },
  },
  {
    eyebrow: "Remote Process",
    title: "A Clear Remote Preparation Process",
    steps: [
      {
        title: "Initial Consultation",
        text:
          "Discuss the business structure, tax year, states involved, and filing needs.",
      },
      {
        title: "Scope Review",
        text:
          "Milana identifies the likely return type and general records required.",
      },
      {
        title: "Engagement and Pricing",
        text:
          "The scope and pricing are confirmed based on the complexity of the business return.",
      },
      {
        title: "Secure Document Collection",
        text:
          "Business records are provided through the approved secure process.",
      },
      {
        title: "Preparation and Questions",
        text:
          "Milana reviews the records and follows up regarding missing or unclear information.",
      },
      {
        title: "Completion",
        text:
          "The business return and applicable owner, shareholder, or partner documents are completed.",
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    eyebrow: "Service Boundaries",
    title: "Important Business-Service Boundaries",
    paragraphs: [
      "Business tax preparation does not automatically include the following services:",
